cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "PACT: Reference Implementation and Evaluation Harness for an AI Accountability Protocol"
message: "If you use this software, the corpus, or the jury-independence measurement, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Shinde
    given-names: Saish Sanjay
    email: saish.shinde@sjsu.edu
    affiliation: San José State University
repository-code: "https://github.com/saish-shinde-007/pact-paper"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation and evaluation harness for PACT, a protocol that makes
  deployed AI conduct non-repudiable and adjudicable among mutually distrusting
  parties. Includes a hash-chained evidence log with witness-cosigned Merkle
  checkpoints, a diversity-constrained commit-reveal jury protocol, a precedent
  graph, and the experiment harness behind the paper's results — notably that
  juror error correlation is judgment rather than lineage (cross-vendor pairs as
  correlated as within-vendor across 19 jurors from 9 vendors, two prompt framings
  and two label sets), concentrated on the cases pre-labelled contested, and that
  aggregation buys containment but never accuracy: every voting rule scores below
  the best single juror once the corpus labels are corrected.
keywords:
  - AI accountability
  - LLM-as-judge
  - transparency logs
  - adjudication protocols
  - AI auditing
  - evaluator ensembles
license: Apache-2.0
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-12"
